FS_UTILS(3)

# NAME

fs\_utils - filesystem utility functions

# SYNOPSIS

```
#include <libpkgcore/fs_utils.h>

std::string mtos(mode_t mode);
std::string trim_filename(const std::string& filename);
bool file_exists(const std::string& filename);
bool file_empty(const std::string& filename);
bool file_equal(const std::string& file1, const std::string& file2);
bool permissions_equal(const std::string& file1, const std::string& file2);
void file_remove(const std::string& basedir, const std::string& filename);
```

# DESCRIPTION

*fs\_utils* provides helper functions for filesystem inspection,
comparison, and mutation.

# FUNCTIONS

*mtos()*
	Converts a mode_t into an ls(1)-style string.

*trim_filename()*
	Normalizes paths by removing redundant slashes.

*file_exists()*
	Returns true if path exists.

*file_empty()*
	Returns true if path is an empty regular file.

*file_equal()*
	Compares file contents.

*permissions_equal()*
	Compares mode, UID, and GID.

*file_remove()*
	Recursively removes a file or directory relative to basedir.

# NOTES

*file_remove()* performs destructive operations without rollback.

Callers must ensure correctness of paths.

# SEE ALSO

*stat*(2),
*unlink*(2),
*db\_lock*(3),
*pkgutil*(3),
